From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:48:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Add the boot options of the payload to the
 setup

Two switches in a "Boot" form of the General category, for the boot
options EDK2 registers from its firmware volume: "Network boot (iPXE)"
(ipxe_boot) and "Legacy boot (CSMWrap)" (csmwrap_boot), each shown only
when its payload option is built in (EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE,
EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP), both on by default. coreboot does not read them:
the boot manager of the payload does, from the variables the setup keeps
them in, and leaves the boot option out when one is off.

TEST=Built for Lenovo ThinkPad W541; the form in the setup on QEMU q35.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 94aaed170..db38ee470 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -203,6 +203,43 @@ static const struct sm_object general_about = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	},
 });
 
+/*
+ * The boot options of the payload: its boot manager reads them (EDK2,
+ * PlatformBootManagerLib), coreboot does not.
+ */
+static const struct sm_object ipxe_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "ipxe_boot",
+	.ui_name	= "Network boot (iPXE)",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The iPXE entry of the boot menu (ESC at power on): PXE,\n"
+			  "HTTP and iPXE scripts over the Ethernet port. Off, the\n"
+			  "entry goes.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+static const struct sm_object csmwrap_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "csmwrap_boot",
+	.ui_name	= "Legacy boot (CSMWrap)",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The CSMWrap entry of the boot menu: a legacy BIOS (the\n"
+			  "CSM of SeaBIOS) for the operating systems and tools that\n"
+			  "do not boot from UEFI, from the disks and USB drives.\n"
+			  "Needs Secure Boot off: while it is on the entry goes\n"
+			  "and the firmware refuses to start CSMWrap.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+static const struct sm_object general_boot = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
+	.flags		= (CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) || CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP))
+			  ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.ui_name	= "Boot",
+	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
+		&ipxe_boot,
+		&csmwrap_boot,
+		NULL
+	},
+});
+
 static const struct sm_object general_sound = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Sound",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
@@ -510,6 +547,7 @@ static struct sm_obj_form general = {
 	.ui_name = "General",
 	.obj_list = (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&general_about,
+		&general_boot,
 		&general_sound,
 		&general_advanced,
 		NULL
-- 
